
%9Syntax:%9

@SYNTAX:credential@

%9Parameters:%9

    PASSWD:     Sets the master password for this session and unlocks
                credentials that were encrypted by an earlier version.
    LIST:       Lists the stored credentials. SASL user names are shown;
                passwords and autosendcmd values are shown as '***'.
    STATUS:     Displays the storage mode, the external file name, whether
                encryption is enabled and whether a master password is set.
    MIGRATE:    CONFIG moves credentials from the external file back into
                the main configuration file. EXTERNAL is refused (see below).
    ENCRYPT:    Refused (see below).
    DECRYPT:    Stores credentials that are encrypted in plain text again.
    RELOAD:     Reloads the credentials from the external file.

    Without any parameter, a short summary of the commands and settings is
    displayed.

%9Description:%9

    Shows and manages the credentials of your networks and servers: server
    passwords, the SASL user name and password of a network, and
    autosendcmd values that contain a login. They are added and removed
    with the normal commands, NETWORK ADD -sasl_username and
    -sasl_password, or SERVER ADD -password.

    Credentials are kept in ~/.erssi/config, which erssi writes readable
    only by you (mode 0600).

    Encryption and the external credentials file are disabled in this
    version: encryption never reached the configuration file (passwords
    stayed in plain text in it), the external mode put them back into it,
    and a wrong master password could delete stored credentials. Turning
    them on - with ENCRYPT, MIGRATE EXTERNAL or /SET - is refused with a
    message. A configuration that already uses them keeps working, so
    nothing stored before is lost; use DECRYPT and MIGRATE CONFIG to go
    back to plain credentials in the configuration file.

    Settings:

        credential_storage_mode (default: config)
        credential_external_file (default: .credentials)
        credential_config_encrypt (default: OFF)

%9Examples:%9

    /CREDENTIAL STATUS
    /CREDENTIAL LIST
    /CREDENTIAL DECRYPT
    /CREDENTIAL MIGRATE CONFIG

%9See also:%9 NETWORK, SAVE, SERVER, SET
